[200.766921, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_trainer.py\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K        self.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio = args.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio\r\n"]
[200.767023, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_config.py\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K        \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio (`float`, defaults to 0.25):\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_config.py\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K            The ratio between the target reward margin (\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K) and beta in SimPO loss.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_config.py\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio: float = 0.25\r\n"]
[200.767549, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/README.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K  - [SimPO trainer](https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO/blob/main/scripts/simpo_trainer.py) update for better reproducibility. The hyperparameter `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K` changed to `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio` for easier tuning.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/README.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KHyperparameter tuning is crucial for SimPO (and other preference optimization algorithms in general). The three main hyperparameters of SimPO to focus on are `learning_rate`, `beta`, and `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K` (we recommend keeping the total batch size fixed at 128).\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/README.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K`: Gamma controls the target reward margin. We suggest tuning the ratio of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K to beta (i.e., `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K / beta`). We recommend using `0.5` as a starting point for `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio` and grid searching between `0` and `1`. A well-tuned `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio` can provide a modest improvement, but it is not as critical as other hyperparameters.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/README.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KWe used the following hyperparameters for training the released models (note that in our latest update, we changed the hyperparameter `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K` to `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio` as the latter is normalized and easier to tune under different `beta` values).\r\n"]
[200.768433, "o", "grep: /root/SimPO/paper.pdf: binary file matches\r\n"]
[200.771563, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/training_configs/mistral-7b-instruct-simpo.yaml\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio: 0.1\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/training_configs/gemma-2-9b-it-simpo.yaml\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio: 0.5\r\n"]
[200.771597, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/training_configs/llama-3-8b-instruct-simpo-v2.yaml\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio: 0.3\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/training_configs/llama-3-8b-base-simpo.yaml\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio: 0.5\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/training_configs/mistral-7b-base-simpo.yaml\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio: 0.8\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/root/SimPO/training_configs/llama-3-8b-instruct-simpo.yaml\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgamma\u001b[m\u001b[K_beta_ratio: 0.55\r\n"]
[200.771812, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@b0c59cfb741c:~# "]
[225.569259, "i", "cat <<EOF > /root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_trainer.py.patch\n@@ -557,11 +557,25 @@\n-    def simpo_loss(\n-        self,\n-        policy_chosen_logps: torch.FloatTensor,\n-        policy_rejected_logps: torch.FloatTensor,\n-    ) -> Tuple[torch.FloatTensor, torch.FloatTensor, torch.FloatTensor]:\n-        \"\"\"Compute the SimPO loss for a batch of policy model log probabilities.\n-\n-        Args:\n-            policy_chosen_logps: Log probabilities of the policy model for the chosen responses. Shape: (batch_size,)\n-            policy_rejected_logps: Log probabilities of the policy model for the rejected responses. Shape: (batch_size,)\n-\n-        Returns:\n-            A tuple of three tensors: (losses, chosen_rewards, rejected_rewards).\n-            The losses tensor contains the SimPO loss for each example in the batch.\n-            The chosen_rewards and rejected_rewards tensors contain the rewards for the chosen and rejected responses, respectively.\n-        \"\"\"\n-\n-        return losses, chosen_rewards, rejected_rewards\n+    def simpo_loss(\n+        self,\n+        policy_chosen_logps: torch.FloatTensor,\n+        policy_rejected_logps: torch.FloatTensor,\n+    ) -> Tuple[torch.FloatTensor, torch.FloatTensor, torch.FloatTensor]:\n+        \"\"\"Compute the SimPO loss for a batch of policy model log probabilities.\n+\n+        Args:\n+            policy_chosen_logps: Log probabilities of the policy model for the chosen responses. Shape: (batch_size,)\n+            policy_rejected_logps: Log probabilities of the policy model for the rejected responses. Shape: (batch_size,)\n+\n+        Returns:\n+            A tuple of three tensors: (losses, chosen_rewards, rejected_rewards).\n+            The losses tensor contains the SimPO loss for each example in the batch.\n+            The chosen_rewards and rejected_rewards tensors contain the rewards for the chosen and rejected responses, respectively.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        pi_logps = policy_chosen_logps - policy_rejected_logps\n+        gamma = self.gamma_beta_ratio * self.beta\n+        logits = self.beta * pi_logps - gamma\n+\n+        if self.loss_type == \"sigmoid\":\n+            losses = (\n+                -F.logsigmoid(logits) * (1 - self.label_smoothing)\n+                - F.logsigmoid(-logits) * self.label_smoothing\n+            )\n+        elif self.loss_type == \"hinge\":\n+            losses = torch.relu(1 - logits)\n+        else:\n+            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown loss type: {self.loss_type}. Should be one of ['sigmoid', 'hinge']\")\n+\n+        chosen_rewards = self.beta * policy_chosen_logps\n+        rejected_rewards = self.beta * policy_rejected_logps\n+\n+        return losses, chosen_rewards, rejected_rewards\nEOF\n"]
